{
  "info": {
    "name": "Healthcare API Tests",
    "description": "# Healthcare API Tests\n\nPostman tests and documentation for the Healthcare REST API of our Full DevOps Lab project (Express, Node.js). The API manages doctors, patients and appointments, and reports metrics. Data is kept in memory: it resets when the server restarts.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. `npm install` once (the repository's `.npmrc` sets `legacy-peer-deps`), then `npm run dev`. The server listens on `http://localhost:3000`.\n2. Import this file in Postman (*Import*). There is no environment or variable to set: every request carries its full address, `http://localhost:3000/api/...`.\n3. *Run collection* in order: later requests reuse the ids saved by earlier ones, and the metrics check compares counts taken before the POST requests, so the run can be repeated on the same server.\n\nThe folder **Lab 5 requests** holds the 8 requests of the lab. The folder **Error cases** has one request for each other documented error, each with its saved answer.\n\nFrom the command line: `npx newman run \"postman/Healthcare API Postman Collection.json\"`.\n\n## Conventions\n\n| Topic | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Format | JSON in and out; send `Content-Type: application/json` with a body. |\n| Ids | Whole numbers given by the server: one more than the highest id in the list. |\n| Dates | `YYYY-MM-DD`, and a real calendar day (`2026-02-30` is refused). |\n| Authentication | None in this lab. |\n\n## Errors\n\n| HTTP | Body | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| 400 | `{ \"error\": \"Missing required fields\" }` | A required field is absent, `null` or empty. `0` counts as present. |\n| 400 | `{ \"error\": \"<field> must be …\" }` | A field is present but has the wrong form (age, date). |\n| 400 | `{ \"error\": true, \"message\": \"…\" }` | The body is not valid JSON (global error handler). |\n| 404 | `{ \"error\": \"Doctor or patient not found\" }` | An appointment names an id that does not exist. |\n| 500 | `{ \"error\": true, \"message\": \"…\" }` | Unexpected server error (global error handler). |\n\n## Endpoints\n\n| Method | Path | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| GET | /api/doctors | List the doctors |\n| POST | /api/doctors | Add a doctor |\n| GET | /api/patients | List the patients |\n| POST | /api/patients | Add a patient |\n| GET | /api/appointments | List the appointments |\n| POST | /api/appointments | Book a visit between a doctor and a patient |\n| GET | /api/metrics | Hospital counts and system stats |\n\nEvery request below has tests (*Scripts → Post-response*): the status code, the shape of the answer and the rule it documents. Each request also has a saved example response from a real run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
